    "problem_statement": "# AND operation missing in QueryInstance class\n\n## Description\n\nThe `__and__` method is missing from the `QueryInstance` class in the `queries.py` file. This method is responsible for implementing the `&` operator between two query instances.\n\nWhen trying to use the `&` operator to combine two queries, the following error occurs:\n\n```\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for &: 'QueryInstance' and 'QueryInstance'\n```\n\nThis affects all query operations that rely on the AND operator, including:\n- Combining two queries with the `&` operator\n- Using path queries with AND conditions\n- Using the NOT operator (`~`) followed by an AND operation\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\nHere's a simple example that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB, Query\n\ndb = TinyDB('db.json')\nUser = Query()\n\n# This will fail with TypeError\nquery = (User.age > 18) & (User.name == 'John')\nresult = db.search(query)\n```\n\nAnother example showing the issue with path queries:\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB, Query\n\ndb = TinyDB('db.json')\nq = Query()\n\n# This will fail with TypeError\nquery = q.value.exists() & (q.value == 5)\nresult = db.search(query)\n```\n\nThe issue affects all operations that internally use the AND operator, breaking a core functionality of the query system."
  }
